      <h2 id="stack">How to build a sensible stack</h2>

      <p>Order of operations, assuming no red-flag symptoms:</p>

      <ol>
        <li><strong>Get vitamin D tested.</strong> If you are deficient, correct it first. It is the cheapest intervention with the highest chance of mattering.</li>
        <li><strong>Add collagen peptides at 5–10g daily.</strong> This is the load-bearing part of the stack. Give it a full 12 weeks.</li>
        <li><strong>Ensure calcium and magnesium are adequate</strong> — via diet if possible. Magnesium is required to convert vitamin D to its active form and is commonly under-consumed.</li>
        <li><strong>Consider bioavailable curcumin</strong> if inflammatory pain is prominent, particularly pain that is worse after activity.</li>
        <li><strong>Reassess at 12 weeks.</strong> Anything that has not helped by then is unlikely to start.</li>
      </ol>

